    "EX-2026-003": {
      "title": "Expense Submission Guidelines",
      "text": "CF SUMMIT 2026 | SYNTHETIC DEMO DATA | NOT A REAL COMPANY POLICY\nPage 1\nExpense Submission Guidelines\nEquipment-related expenses during business travel\nDocument ID\nEX-2026-003\nTenant\ncompany-a\nVersion\n1.0\nStatus\nAPPROVED\nEffective from\n2026-01-01\nEffective through\nUntil superseded\nAudience\nall-staff\nCurrent\ntrue\n1. Before spending\nEmployees must obtain written IT authorization before purchasing replacement computing equipment. Finance\nchecks supporting documentation but does not replace the IT approval required by EQ-2026-007.\n2. Supporting evidence\nAttach the itemized receipt, currency, purchase date, incident reference, travel approval reference and written IT\nauthorization to the expense claim. Finance may request clarification before processing.\n3. Eligibility and exclusions\nSubmitting a receipt does not guarantee reimbursement. Personally owned computing devices are excluded\nfrom the company equipment replacement process. Only approved, eligible expenses proceed to Finance\nreview.\n4. Missing limits\nThis document does not specify a fixed equipment reimbursement cap. No approved 2027 laptop\nreimbursement limit is supplied in this corpus. If asked for an unsupported amount, refer the employee to\nFinance rather than infer a number from an unrelated document.\n5. Owner and dependencies\nGuideline owner: Finance Operations. Read with EQ-2026-007 and TR-2026-002. Live approval status and\npayment status are held in business systems, not in this document.\n",
